tasks.official_scoring_standard:
Execution-based scoring: run the submitted solution and verify it meets the success criteria below. Award the four DERBench L3 capability dimensions (Information Extraction, Domain Reasoning, Multi-Objective Decision Making, Uncertainty & Adaptation), 0-25 each (max 100), based on correctness, method validity, and completeness.

Success criteria: {"must_output": ["per_home_flexibility_table", "ranked_list_with_composite_scores", "flexibility_envelope_plots_top3"], "must_include_columns": ["home_id", "max_kw_reduction", "max_duration_hrs", "energy_capacity_kwh", "recovery_peak_kw", "recovery_duration_hrs", "composite_score", "rank"]}

Reference solution: Expected ranking (approximate): Homes with high thermal mass and large temperature deadband (H04, H10, H07) should rank highest due to their ability to sustain load reduction for longer. H04 (5.0 ton, high thermal mass, 4 degC deadband) should have: max_kw_reduction ~4.5 kW (5.8 * 0.78 duty cycle), max_duration ~13.3 hrs (4 degC / 0.3 degC/hr), energy_capacity ~60 kWh, but capped at practical 4 hours for DR events yielding 18 kWh usable. H06 (low thermal mass, only 1 degC deadband) should rank lowest: max_duration ~1.25 hrs (1 / 0.8), limited energy capacity. The agent must correctly estimate duty cycles from consumption data, apply the thermal model, compute all metrics, produce the ranking table, and generate clear visualizations.
